course: dictionary
lesson: 5417
title: Lactic: a milk word and a muscle word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special topic, like science or sport. «Lactic» is one of them. Its clue is in the word itself: lactic means to do with milk, so a lactic acid is an acid linked to milk.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Bacteria in yoghurt turn milk sugar into lactic acid, which makes it thick and tangy.» The words milk, yoghurt and thick tell you that lactic acid comes from milk. Tangy means having a sharp, sour taste.
explain: Now look at a sports sentence: «Lactic acid is cleared within about an hour after exercise, so it does not cause next-day soreness.» Exercise tells you lactic acid is also made in your muscles. The word so tells you the result: it is gone quickly, so it is not the reason you ache the next day.
fact: Lactic means to do with milk.
fact: Lactic acid is made when milk goes sour, for example when friendly bacteria turn milk into yoghurt.
fact: Your muscles also make lactic acid during hard exercise, such as sprinting.
fact: «Soreness a day or two after a race comes from tiny muscle strains being repaired», not from lactic acid.
fact: «Lactose» is the sugar in milk, and people who cannot digest it are «lactose intolerant».
exercise: «Bacteria in yoghurt turn milk sugar into lactic acid, which makes it thick and tangy.» Which words show that lactic acid comes from milk? | Bacteria and acid | Turn and makes | Thick and tangy | *Milk sugar and yoghurt
exercise: «Lactic acid is cleared within about an hour after exercise, so it does not cause next-day soreness.» What does this tell you? | It makes your muscles grow | *It is gone within about an hour | It stays in your muscles for days | It is only found in yoghurt
exercise: Ella thinks lactic means fast, like a sprint. What clue in the yoghurt sentence shows she is wrong? | The word yoghurt is long | The word sprint is not in the sentence | *Milk and yoghurt show it is about milk | It has the letter c in it
test: Dan says, «Soreness a day or two after a race comes from tiny muscle strains being repaired.» Does lactic acid cause this soreness? | Only if you drink milk | *No, the soreness comes from muscle strains being repaired | Yes, it lasts for days | Yes, it is in the yoghurt
test: On a yoghurt pot, «live cultures» means what? | The pot is alive | Milk is not allowed in it | *Friendly bacteria are still in the yoghurt | Tiny plants grow in the milk
exam: Lactic acid is made when milk goes sour, as in yoghurt. What does lactic acid make the milk? | *Thick and tangy | Bubbly and fizzy | Pink and sweet | Cold and frozen
